{
  "__readme": "Shared fixtures for the per-trial FRICTION SIGNALS contract (version 1). Loaded by sdk/tests/friction-signals.test.ts. LOAD RULE: strip EVERY key whose name starts with '__' before handing a row to a validator. Signals are OBSERVATIONS, never verdicts, and these rows pin the validator that says so. No customer tool names, no identifier VALUES — key paths and counts only. Synthetic tools are search_issues, get_issue, list_pages.",
  "__tuning": [
    "The identifier rules — IDENTIFIER_KEY_RE, ID_LIKE_LITERAL_RE and MIN_IDENTIFIER_LENGTH — are the tunable surface of this contract, and the PR1a labelling round moves them and nothing else.",
    "Every tuning change gets a row here with a `__why` naming the labelled trials that forced it, so a later reader can tell a rule that was measured from one that was guessed.",
    "v1 initial: no tuning change yet. ID_LIKE_LITERAL_RE is the backend authoring-lint regex widened by ULID and bare hex (>= 8 chars); MIN_IDENTIFIER_LENGTH is 3 because a two-character candidate matches inside most timestamps and offsets, which suppresses the signal it belongs to."
  ],
  "accept": [
    {
